<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al-Zubayr Rahma Mansur</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Al-Zubayr</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Zubayr Rahma Mansur was a Sudanese slave-trading merchant and warlord of the nineteenth century who built a powerful private army in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahr-al-ghazal">Bahr al-Ghazal</a> region. Operating with tacit Egyptian backing, he invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur</a> in 1874. His defeat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Ibrahim in October 1874 ended the first Darfur Sultanate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-zubayr-rahma-mansur.jpg" alt="Al-Zubayr Rahma Mansur" width="300" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SLATIN(1896)_p079_ZUBEIR_PASHA_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
